{"schemaVersion":1,"kind":"error","classification":"planning","code":"PROMPT_CLARIFICATION_REQUIRED","message":"Headless execution requires clarification before a repository plan can be created.","promptUnderstanding":{"schemaVersion":1,"promptId":"84c9f7391d1c2748fbfffe9d786b8aaa84c9f7391d1c2748fbfffe9d786b8aaa","inputId":"6700a26129b0bba82b8bfce1f6258a366700a26129b0bba82b8bfce1f6258a36","outcome":"repository_action","readiness":"clarification_required","reply":"I need the failing verifier evidence before the bounded fix can be defined safely. The requested behavior is ambiguous without the observed failure or expected percentage semantics.","conversationSummary":"The user requests a repository-only bounded implementation for percentage behavior. Allowed writer paths are src/calculator.ts and test/calculator.test.ts; .env, .git/**, and bun.lock are protected. No other files may be modified. Run bun test when execution is appropriate. The failing verifier evidence has not been provided.","refinedBrief":{"goal":"Implement the percentage behavior indicated by the failing verifier evidence.","deliverables":["A bounded fix in src/calculator.ts if required.","A regression test in test/calculator.test.ts if required.","bun test execution when appropriate."],"constraints":["Modify only src/calculator.ts and test/calculator.test.ts.","Do not modify .env, .git/**, bun.lock, or any other file.","Use the failing verifier evidence to define the behavior.","Retry only the bounded fix."],"acceptanceCriteria":["The supplied verifier failure is resolved.","The percentage behavior is covered by the allowed test file when a regression test is appropriate.","bun test passes when it can be run."],"nonGoals":["Do not change files outside the two allowed writer paths.","Do not perform unrelated refactors or retries."]},"questions":[{"id":"verifier_evidence","prompt":"What failing verifier evidence should define the percentage behavior to implement?","rationale":"The evidence is necessary to distinguish the intended percentage semantics and keep the fix bounded.","kind":"outcome","options":[{"id":"paste_failure","label":"Paste failure","description":"Provide the verifier output, failing test, or assertion details.","recommended":true},{"id":"describe_expected","label":"Describe behavior","description":"State the expected percentage inputs and outputs.","recommended":false}]}],"assumptions":[]}}
